  "scientific_summary": "336276 independent ordinary PASS, exact model binding PASS and cached source PASS for the literal: for every fixed k>=2 the expected k-width of a sequence of n iid uniform-endpoint intervals, divided by n, tends to 1/(k+1). Supplied arXiv v5 and DMTCS 22:1 (2020) #17 PDFs are byte-identical. The source k=1 square-root sentence is a real source error, because intervals covering 1/2 already form an antichain of expected size n/2; the review reports that the companion describes the square-root formula as a longest-chain statistic, and no credit attaches to that correction. Companion 1802.03436v2 was read in full and repeats the conjecture as Conjecture 20 without proof; Huang-Sellier ESA 2022 is a theorem-level nonmatch. No earlier interval-limit proof or complete routine reduction was identified within a bounded search of two calls and six strings; no worldwide novelty claim. Root prospective scientific PASS on the reviewer recommendation CREDITABLE SUBJECT TO LEAN AND PAPER: the all-time-cut suffix-maxima block envelope is the substantive step beyond the source Hall representation, with modest methodological novelty. The routine dense-matching LLN objection is retained and may be revisited if an applicable primary theorem appears. Credit 0. Acceptance requires a literal Lean endpoint, independent formal, source and body audit, paper, clean extracted replay and root final adjudication. All 96 supplied scopes compared, no family overlap, one prospective family. 145 manifest files, 32 frozen bindings verified; one documentary KeyError retained.",
